{"case_id": "m02", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "**LCM of 12 and 18**\n\nPrime factorisation:  \n12 = 2² × 3  \n18 = 2 × 3²  \n\nLCM = product of the highest powers of all primes present  \n= 2² × 3²  \n= 4 × 9  \n= 36  \n\n**Answer:** 36", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.046, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 378, "output_tokens": 184, "reasoning_tokens": 88, "cost_usd": 0.000616, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:45"}
{"case_id": "m03", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "**Step 1: Find the total number of parts**  \nRatio = 2 : 3 : 4  \nTotal parts = 2 + 3 + 4 = 9\n\n**Step 2: Find the value of one part**  \nTotal amount = R360  \nValue of one part = R360 ÷ 9 = R40\n\n**Step 3: Determine the largest share**  \nThe largest share corresponds to the ratio part 4.  \nLargest share = 4 × R40 = R160\n\n**Final answer:** R160", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.99, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 464, "output_tokens": 264, "reasoning_tokens": 132, "cost_usd": 0.000814, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:46"}
{"case_id": "m04", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "**Solution:**\n\nAverage speed is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute the given values:\n\\[\n\\text{Speed} = \\frac{240\\ \\text{km}}{3\\ \\text{h}}\n\\]\n\nCalculate:\n\\[\n\\text{Speed} = 80\\ \\text{km/h}\n\\]\n\n**Final answer:** \\( 80\\ \\text{km/h} \\)", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 6.065, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 441, "output_tokens": 165, "reasoning_tokens": 69, "cost_usd": 0.000805, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["DigitalOcean"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:48"}
{"case_id": "m01", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "**Solution:**\nPrime factorisation of 84:  \n84 = 2 × 42 = 2 × 2 × 21 = 2² × 3 × 7\n\nPrime factorisation of 126:  \n126 = 2 × 63 = 2 × 3 × 21 = 2 × 3 × 3 × 7 = 2 × 3² × 7\n\nCommon prime factors with lowest exponents: 2¹, 3¹, 7¹  \nHCF = 2 × 3 × 7 = 42\n\n**Answer:** 42", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 6.703, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 407, "output_tokens": 364, "reasoning_tokens": 237, "cost_usd": 0.000767, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Baidu"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:48"}
{"case_id": "m05", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "**Simple Interest formula**  \n\\( \\text{SI} = P \\times i \\times n \\)  \n\n**Given:**  \nPrincipal \\( P = \\text{R}5\\,000 \\)  \nInterest rate \\( i = 8\\% = \\frac{8}{100} = 0{,}08 \\)  \nTime \\( n = 3 \\) years  \n\n**Calculation:**  \n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{SI} &= \\text{R}5\\,000 \\times 0{,}08 \\times 3 \\\\\n&= \\text{R}400 \\times 3 \\\\\n&= \\text{R}1\\,200\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n**Answer:**  \nThe simple interest earned is **R1 200**.", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.733, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 520, "reasoning_tokens": 317, "cost_usd": 0.001151, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:48"}
{"case_id": "m41", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "Tₙ = a + (n − 1)d  \nT₂₅ = 7 + (25 − 1)(4)  \n= 7 + 24 × 4  \n= 7 + 96  \n= 103\n\n**Answer:** 103", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.787, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 472, "output_tokens": 106, "reasoning_tokens": 30, "cost_usd": 0.000813, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Cloudflare"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:49"}
{"case_id": "m44", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "**Solution:**\n\nThe series is \\(16 + 8 + 4 + \\cdots\\)\n\nThis is a geometric series with first term \\(a = 16\\) and common ratio \\(r = \\frac{8}{16} = \\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\nSince \\(|r| = \\frac{1}{2} < 1\\), the sum to infinity exists.\n\n\\[\nS_{\\infty} = \\frac{a}{1 - r}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nS_{\\infty} = \\frac{16}{1 - \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{16}{\\frac{1}{2}} = 16 \\times 2 = 32\n\\]\n\n**Final answer:** \\(32\\)", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 2.256, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 279, "reasoning_tokens": 102, "cost_usd": 0.000768, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:51"}
{"case_id": "m43", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "**Step 1: Identify the first term and common ratio**\n\\[\na = 2\n\\]\n\\[\nr = \\frac{6}{2} = 3\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Write the formula for the nth term of a geometric sequence**\n\\[\nT_n = a \\cdot r^{n-1}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Substitute \\( n = 8 \\), \\( a = 2 \\), and \\( r = 3 \\)**\n\\[\nT_8 = 2 \\cdot 3^{8-1} = 2 \\cdot 3^7\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Calculate \\( 3^7 \\)**\n\\[\n3^7 = 2187\n\\]\n\n**Step 5: Multiply by 2**\n\\[\nT_8 = 2 \\cdot 2187 = 4374\n\\]\n\n**Final answer:** \\( 4374 \\)", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 4.041, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 451, "output_tokens": 418, "reasoning_tokens": 144, "cost_usd": 0.001033, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:52"}
{"case_id": "m42", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "**Solution**\n\n1. Identify the type of sequence: The terms 3; 7; 11; … form an arithmetic sequence because there is a constant difference between successive terms.\n\n2. State the first term and common difference:\n   \\[\n   a = 3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   d = 7 - 3 = 4\n   \\]\n\n3. Write the formula for the sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence:\n   \\[\n   S_n = \\frac{n}{2}\\bigl[2a + (n-1)d\\bigr]\n   \\]\n\n4. Substitute \\(n = 20\\), \\(a = 3\\) and \\(d = 4\\) into the formula:\n   \\[\n   S_{20} = \\frac{20}{2}\\bigl[2(3) + (20-1)(4)\\bigr]\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 10\\bigl[6 + 19 \\times 4\\bigr]\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 10\\bigl[6 + 76\\bigr]\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 10 \\times 82\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 820\n   \\]\n\n5. Final answer:\n   \\[\n   S_{20} = 820\n   \\]", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 5.03, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 393, "output_tokens": 525, "reasoning_tokens": 161, "cost_usd": 0.001141, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:53"}
{"case_id": "m45", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "### Solution\n\nThe sum is arithmetic:  \n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{10} (2k+1) = 3 + 5 + 7 + \\cdots + 21\n\\]\n\n- First term: \\(a = 2(1)+1 = 3\\)  \n- Last term: \\(T_{10} = 2(10)+1 = 21\\)  \n- Number of terms: \\(n = 10\\)\n\nUsing the arithmetic sum formula \\(S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(a + T_n)\\):\n\\[\nS_{10} = \\frac{10}{2}(3 + 21) = 5 \\times 24 = 120\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(120\\)", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.878, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 433, "output_tokens": 455, "reasoning_tokens": 189, "cost_usd": 0.001072, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:53"}
{"case_id": "m16", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Geometry of Straight Lines"], "output": "Let the unknown angle be \\(x\\).  \nSince the two angles lie on a straight line, they add up to \\(180^\\circ\\) (angles on a straight line).  \n\n\\[\nx + 125^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = 180^\\circ - 125^\\circ\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = 55^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThe other angle is \\(55^\\circ\\).", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 2.748, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 443, "output_tokens": 159, "reasoning_tokens": 69, "cost_usd": 0.000637, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:05:44"}
{"case_id": "m07", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Exponents"], "output": "### Solution\n\nUsing the law of exponents \\(a^m \\times a^n = a^{m+n}\\):\n\n\\[\n2^3 \\times 2^2 = 2^{3+2} = 2^5 = 32\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** 32", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.707, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 405, "output_tokens": 284, "reasoning_tokens": 194, "cost_usd": 0.00079, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:05:45"}
