{"case_id": "m54", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Differential calculus", "grade12"], "output": "f(x) = 3x⁴ − 2x² + 5x\n\nf′(x) = 3·4x⁴⁻¹ − 2·2x²⁻¹ + 5·1x¹⁻¹\n\nf′(x) = 12x³ − 4x + 5", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 5.517, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 395, "output_tokens": 417, "reasoning_tokens": 223, "cost_usd": 0.000981, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:05:54"}
{"case_id": "m52", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-pro@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Functions and inverse functions", "grade12"], "output": "1. Write \\(y = f(x)\\):\n   \\[\n   y = 3x - 6\n   \\]\n\n2. Interchange \\(x\\) and \\(y\\):\n   \\[\n   x = 3y - 6\n   \\]\n\n3. Solve for \\(y\\):\n   \\[\n   x + 6 = 3y\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{x + 6}{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. Write the inverse function:\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 6}{3} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x}{3} + 2\n   \\]", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 6.751, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 325, "reasoning_tokens": 171, "cost_usd": 0.000512, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"], "hosts": ["StreamLake"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:05:54"}
